; orderlists ($ = hex pattern number in the declarations above): transpose (+n/-n semitones, kept until changed), patterns in
; hex, "loop n" back to entry n or "stop".  Four voices, 32-row patterns:
; intro 4, groove 4, organ 4, bells 2 (double time), key change up 2, 4.
subtune 0 speed=6
order 0.1: +0 00 -4 00 +3 00 -2 00  +0 01 -4 01 +3 01 -2 01  +0 02 -4 02 +3 02 -2 02  +0 03 04  +2 01 -2 01 +5 01 +0 01 stop
order 0.2: 05 05 05 07  06 06 06 07  05 05 06 07  08 06  09 06 06 0A stop
order 0.3: +0 0B -4 0C +3 0C -2 0C  +0 0D -4 0E +3 0E -2 0E  +0 0F -4 10 +3 10 -2 10  +0 1C 11  +2 0D -2 0E +5 0E +0 0E stop
order 0.4: 1C 1C 1C 11  +0 12 13 14 15  16 17 18 19  1A 1B  +2 12 13 14 15 stop

